d3d11: drain the command queue before the device's state is torn down

Applies on top of 0006 (dxmt bcdcf6da + the staging UpdateSubresource path).

MTLD3D11DXGIDevice destroys its d3d11_device_ member (the pipeline cache,
the state object caches, the resources recorded chunks reference) before
`device`, whose CommandQueue keeps its encode and finish threads running
until its own destructor joins them.  A chunk still being encoded then
walks freed state: DWM re-created its D3D11 device right after uploading a
desktop-sized texture (7680x4074, 125 MB, three monitors) and the render
worker died in the encode thread inside a chunk lambda (pointer
authentication failure on a freed capture, 2026-09-21).  The DXGI device's
destructor now commits what the immediate context recorded and waits for
every committed chunk to finish before any member is destroyed.

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_device.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_device.cpp
index 6ad778e..46609c7 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_device.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_device.cpp
@@ -1133,6 +1133,17 @@ private:
   std::unique_ptr<MTLD3D11CommandListPoolBase> commandlist_pool_;
   std::unique_ptr<MTLD3D11PipelineCacheBase> pipeline_cache_;
 
+public:
+  /**
+   * AnyOS: commit whatever the immediate context has recorded, for the
+   * owner to wait on before this device's state is torn down.
+   */
+  void FlushImmediateContextForShutdown() {
+    if (context_)
+      context_->Flush();
+  }
+
+private:
   Device& device_;
   /** ensure destructor called first */
   std::unique_ptr<MTLD3D11DeviceContextBase> context_;
@@ -1167,6 +1178,17 @@ public:
   }
 
   ~MTLD3D11DXGIDevice() {
+    // AnyOS: d3d11_device_ (the pipeline cache, the state object caches,
+    // the resources the recorded chunks reference) is destroyed before
+    // `device`, whose command queue keeps encoding and finishing chunks
+    // on its own threads until its own destructor joins them -- a chunk
+    // still being encoded then walked freed state (the encode thread died
+    // in a chunk lambda while DWM re-created its device right after a
+    // 125 MB desktop-sized upload, 2026-09-21).  Commit what is recorded
+    // and wait for every committed chunk to finish first.
+    d3d11_device_.FlushImmediateContextForShutdown();
+    if (auto committed = cmd_queue_.CurrentSeqId(); committed > 0)
+      cmd_queue_.WaitCPUFence(committed - 1);
     if (local_kmt_) {
       D3DKMT_DESTROYDEVICE destroy = {};
       destroy.hDevice = local_kmt_;
